      "writtenOn": "2021-01-19T16:04:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It looks like this code comes from netd. But that uses unsigned arithmetic and Java arithmetic is always signed. So adding anything to QUOTA_UNLIMITED will not result in overflow. However, it *will* result in something that is \u003c rxBytes + txBytes (specifically, it will result in rxBytes + txBytes - 1), so I think this code is still correct.\n\nWe should update the comment though. Something like:\n\n    // If adding limit caused overflow, or if limit was QUOTA_UNLIMITED, clamp to unlimited.",
      "range": {
